From 3ebbccbc9ed7e1a44c0df201259f87fb93ad10b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "erik.hauan" <erik.hauan@radiantvs.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:26:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] engine-manager: manifest action extensions behind E10

Behaviour: manifests keep the fork's action keys: optional_args (argv
fragments appended for present integer params, cmd actions only),
result.record (typed slots/ctx/bytes extraction, whole-response when array and
field are both empty), result.each/each_field (per loaded instance rows, LM
Studio's loaded_instances) and match.loading_in (loading rows count as
occupied for strict residency), each validated as before.

Seams used: E10 (registry.go: Action embeds LocalActionExt, ActionResult
embeds LocalResultExt, ResultMatch embeds LocalMatchExt, each after NVIDIA's
last field; Action.validate calls a.localValidate(name) just before
upstream's result.array/result.field check, which a record result skips;
each marked // fork:E10; types, regexps and localValidate in
services/nvpair-engine-manager/local_registry.go). NVIDIA's #181 action kinds
(hf_cache, launch_model, hf_pull, stop_engine), advertised_models and
inventory_field are kept verbatim.

Proving tests: TestE10_Nil, TestLocalActionExtValidate, TestOptionalArgv,
TestExtractRecords (nvpair-engine-manager).

Feature-group commit for catch-up step 4, exported as
local/patches/004-engine-manifest-ext.patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
